  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-jscodeshift-utils (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a remote binary. It fingerprints the OS/architecture, then fetches a payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a fallback download channel that reassembles base64 chunks served via DNS TXT records under c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded content is written to a hidden cache file (.cache_\u003chex\u003e in /var/tmp, or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\" on Unix).",
